--- outcome: SURVIVED, retained rather than discarded ---
Baseline 129466cc, before the test was corrected. The uniqueness guard was
removed and `one_receipt_cannot_be_bound_to_two_successions` still passed,
because the second succession in that version was committed but incomplete: the
0120 rule "a row may carry a receipt only once both trailing effects have
landed" refused the planted binding before the uniqueness index was ever
consulted. The split had therefore not actually separated the two guards.

The test now carries the second succession to complete, so the completeness
CHECK passes and uniqueness is the only rule left to refuse. Re-run against
baseline e5aea100 as M-P22b1-receipt-not-unique: killed.

This record is kept because the kill is only meaningful beside it.
